{"id":100,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"An enigmatic Pokémon that happens to bear a resemblance to a Poké Ball. When excited, it discharges the electric current it has stored in its belly, then lets out a great, uproarious laugh."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"It is said to camouflage itself as a Poké Ball. It will self-destruct with very little stimulus."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Voltorb is extremely sensitive—it explodes at the slightest of shocks. It is rumored that it was first created when a Poké Ball was exposed to a powerful pulse of energy."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Voltorb was first sighted at a company that manufactures Poké Balls. The link between that sighting and the fact that this Pokémon looks very similar to a Poké Ball remains a mystery."},{"games":["Y","LeafGreen"],"text":"Usually found in power plants. Easily mistaken for a Poké Ball, it has zapped many people."},{"games":["X","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"It was discovered when Poké Balls were introduced. It is said that there is some connection."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"It looks just like a Poké Ball. It is dangerous because it may electrocute or explode on contact."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It looks just like a Poké Ball. It is dangerous because it may electrocute or explode on touch."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"It rolls to move. If the ground is uneven, a sudden jolt from hitting a bump can cause it to explode."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"A life-form whose identity is unknown. It is said to SCREECH or suddenly SELFDESTRUCT."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"It bears an uncanny and unexplained resemblance to a POKé BALL. Because it explodes at the slightest shock, even veteran TRAINERS treat it with caution."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"During the study of this POKéMON, it was discovered that its components are not found in nature."